[2m╭─[0m[2m───────────────────────────────────────────────────[0m[2m assumptions [0m[2m────────────────────────────────────────────────────[0m[2m─╮[0m
[2m│[0m [2m• EV is per unit staked: probability x decimal payout - 1; decimal payout = 1 / the book's implied probability.[0m      [2m│[0m
[2m│[0m [2m• Legs on different races are independent: the slip probability is the product of their probabilities.[0m               [2m│[0m
[2m│[0m [2m• Legs on the same race are priced jointly from simulations when they are available (passed in, or a stored combo [0m   [2m│[0m
[2m│[0m [2mrun with exactly these legs); otherwise the product of the marginals, flagged 'correlated: EV approximate'.[0m          [2m│[0m
[2m│[0m [2m• The market's slip probability is the product of its legs' prices: no exchange lists the slip itself.[0m               [2m│[0m
[2m│[0m [2m• Model and market are shown side by side, never blended (owner, 2026-10-07).[0m                                        [2m│[0m
[2m│[0m [2m• The market price is the freshest linked exchange's mid (bid/ask midpoint, else its last price, else the tape's).[0m   [2m│[0m
[2m│[0m [2mblend: none (owner, 2026-10-07; docs/sportsbook/slips.md)[0m                                                            [2m│[0m
